-- #822 S1 PIN: the spec's own `gpure`.  `gpure : a -> f ⟨ ⟩ a` is one of the four
-- canonical graded signatures in EFFECTS-SEMANTICS §6, and a CLOSED row is a perfectly
-- good grade — the unit of the join.
--
-- It was rejected: `isRowSlotArg` recognised a written row only when it carried an OPEN
-- tail, so `f <> a` fell to the opaque fallback and drew T-EFFECT-KIND-MISMATCH — a message
-- asserting the slot "isn't row-kinded" when slot 0 of `f` had just been inferred KRow
-- from `gth` in the very same interface.  The identical spelling on a CONCRETE head
-- (`mkPure : a -> Async <> a`, below) was accepted throughout, so the two halves of the
-- feature disagreed on one spelling and the abstract half misdiagnosed why.
--
-- #823 cannot add the graded core interfaces while this is rejected, so it is a
-- workstream blocker, not polish.  Both spellings are checked here so the pair can never
-- drift apart again.
data Async (e : Effect) a = Done a | Suspend (Unit -> <e> Async e a)

mkPure : a -> Async <> a
mkPure x = Done x

interface GT (f : Effect -> Type -> Type) where
  gth : f e a -> (a -> <e> f e b) -> f e b
  gpure : a -> f <> a
